THE KARNATAKA STATE INDUSTRIAL AREAS  DEVELOPMENT BOARD,
 KHANIJA BHAVAN, RACE COURSE ROAD,
 BENGALURU - 560 001.
 REPRESENTED BY ITS CEO,
 (R19 IMPLEADED V.C.O DATED 28.10.2022  ...RESPONDENTS (BY SRI. R SRINIVASA GOWDA., AGA FOR R1 & R2;
 SRI.N N HARISH., ADVOCATE FOR R3 & R4;
 SRI. B B PATIL., ADVOCATE FOR R5 & R19;
 SRI. AJAY N NANDALIKE., ADVOCATE FOR R8 TO R15;
 SRI. VARUN R R., ADVOCATE FOR R16 & R17;
 R6,R7 & R18 ARE SERVED AND UNREPRESENTED)
 THIS WRIT PETITION IS FILED UNDER ARTICLE 226 OF THE CONSTITUTION OF INDIA, PRAYING TO QUASH THE ORDER DTD.11.3.2022 PASSED BY THE R-7 AT ANNEXURE-R IN SO FAR AS IT RELATES TO THE RECOMMENDATION TO INCLUDE THE NAME OF THE R-16 IN THE FINAL DECLARATION UNDER SEC.28(4) NOTIFICATION AND TREATING 645.48 SQ MTRS AS ENCROACHMENT AND ETC.,

SRI. B B PATIL., ADVOCATE FOR R2 & R3;
 SRI. ASHOK B PATIL., ADVOCATE FOR R5;
Shaik Abdul Rahman vs The State Of Karnataka on 12 April, 2023 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/43034005/

In these two writ petitions, both the sides having argued the matter at length, now graciously agree with the suggestion of the Court as under:
(1) the respondent-SLAO shall frame the award at the earliest send award notice to the persons interested, and deposit the compensation amount in the jurisdictional court within an outer limit of eight weeks;
(2) the SLAO shall refer the rival claims to the above Court for the adjudication under Section 64 of the Right to Fair Compensation and Transparency, Resettlement and Rehabilitation, Act, 2013;
(3) the jurisdictional Court shall after notice to all the stakeholders adjudicate upon the claims/ rival claims for compensation in accordance with law and within an outer limit of three months, from the date the reference is made by the SLAO.

opennyai_summary.decision:
In these two writ petitions, both the sides having argued the matter at length, now graciously agree with the suggestion of the Court as under:
(1) the respondent-SLAO shall frame the award at the earliest send award notice to the persons interested, and deposit the compensation amount in the jurisdictional court within an outer limit of eight weeks;
(2) the SLAO shall refer the rival claims to the above Court for the adjudication under Section 64 of the Right to Fair Compensation and Transparency, Resettlement and Rehabilitation, Act, 2013;
(3) the jurisdictional Court shall after notice to all the stakeholders adjudicate upon the claims/ rival claims for compensation in accordance with law and within an outer limit of three months, from the date the reference is made by the SLAO.
The release of compensation amount shall depend upon the outcome of such adjudication;
(4) the parties whose claim for release of compensation has been favoured, may seek enhancement of compensation;
(5) all contentions of the parties in the adjudication of the rival claims for compensation and for the enhancement of compensation are kept open.
Ordered accordingly and these Writ Petitions are disposed off, costs having been made easy.

